\ RV32I spec test (TODO 5.6/5.7): drive edge vectors through the single-entry rvstep microcode and
\ compare each 32-bit result against an offline reference (computed independently, baked below).
\ x3 = x1 OP (x2 for R-type / imm for I-type). Self-checking: prints OK per vector, or FAIL with
\ got/want. Golden is all OK, so any regression in the decode, opcode/funct3/funct7 dispatch, immediate
\ sign-extension, or an ALU op flips a line and fails make golden.
hex
variable WLO  variable WHI
: seedr rv-idx ! rv-rhi ! rv-rlo ! rvwr ;             ( lo hi idx -- )
: chk ( alo ahi blo bhi irlo irhi wlo whi -- )
  WHI ! WLO !  rv-ih ! rv-il !
  02 seedr  01 seedr
  rvstep  03 rv-idx ! rvrd
  rv-s1hi @ WHI @ =  rv-s1lo @ WLO @ =  and
  if ." OK" else ." FAIL got=" rv-s1hi @ u. rv-s1lo @ u. ." want=" WHI @ u. WLO @ u. then cr ;
FFFF 0000 0001 0000 81B3 0020 0000 0001 chk  \ ADD 0000FFFF = 00010000
FFFF FFFF 0001 0000 81B3 0020 0000 0000 chk  \ ADD FFFFFFFF = 00000000
FFFF 7FFF 0001 0000 81B3 0020 0000 8000 chk  \ ADD 7FFFFFFF = 80000000
0000 8000 0000 8000 81B3 0020 0000 0000 chk  \ ADD 80000000 = 00000000
